A||N||10||Ditz88GT||Subwoofer size and make||||5
Z||000000||Ditz88GT||11-11-1999||12:33 PM||||I finally found someone who will sell me a subwoofer kit, but the speaker is blown.  I was wondering if anyone else out there has replaced the speaker.  I'm not even totally sure what size it is. I've heard everything from 5" to 8".  Also I want to put a good speaker in it, what would you recomend?||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||11-11-1999||01:46 PM||||I just pulled mine out. I measured it at 5 inches. I replaced mine for $38 from speaker city in los angeles||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||11-12-1999||12:02 AM||||Tom, was it an exact replacement?<BR>There's a shop here (in Atlanta) that can repair speakers where the foam has dissolved, but they couldn't come up with a replacement.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JIM GOOSE||11-12-1999||08:36 AM||||You are going to have a hard time finding an exact replacement(I've been looking). All the factory subwoofer stuff is discontinued & of course, its oneofakind oddball pieces. The sub driveris listed as 5.25" though its more like 5" and appears to have a 28oz magnet<BR>(app.)with whole spkr wt. at 2lb2oz.. I've found a mid/bass and am adapting it to the box so havent heard it yet.  I think the main problem you'll have is getting the replacement to go into the box, because the o.d. will be greater than the original.  If this works acceptably, I'd be willing to sell this speaker for 30$ with instructions. Contact me at <A HREF="http://www.hamptonmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.hamptonmotorsports.com</A>  if interested.||||reg||3
Z||000004||Greg Piet||11-12-1999||11:54 AM||||Tom,<BR>could you post the number to speaker city, and thier stock # for the replacement speaker?||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||11-12-1999||12:02 PM||||It is a direct replacement<BR>Speaker City 818 846 9921<BR>Versa-Tronics   D0B130R-PP/8<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ditz88GT||11-12-1999||12:50 PM||||Doesn't anyone else make a speaker in that size?  I was hoping to go with something a little stronger than the OEM.  Has anyone tried altering the box to fit a better speaker?||||reg||5
Z||000007||TOM||11-12-1999||08:22 PM||||Making a bigger/better speaker fit in the stock box would be pretty easy||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||11-12-1999||11:51 PM||||Seems like once when I was surfing the 'net, I ran across somebody who had modified the Fiero factory subwoofer box and fitted a standard 8 incher into it. Of course, I didn't bookmark that page. Trouble is, you'll have to use a subwoofer that'll work in a very small box. Not all subs will do that.||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||11-12-1999||11:55 PM||||After posting that last comment, I started thinking more about it. Maybe I was mistaken about the 8 inch sub, it might of been a standard 6 inch sub the Fiero box was modified for. The 6 inch subs are not as common as the 8 inchers, but still available I believe.||||reg||1
Z||000010||JIM GOOSE||11-15-1999||03:48 PM||||If you put a different size driver (6-8") on the FIERO sub box, you will have a whole "nother animal. The reason the box is so weird in shape is volume matched to the driver itself. Supposedly, any 5.25" should match the bolt pattern though diameter may prevent it fitting into the box like the stock one. If the VERSATRONIC fits inside the box and the grille fits like stock, better go for it.  Ive adapted another driver to my box but had to modify it along the way which was a little tedious. You can get the stock sub re-coned for abt 30$ & this might be best.||||reg||1
